From 27ef91dd68c3c48ab7e0157a93bb0b9ff2108366 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:37:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(#22): the census is per candidate site, each mutant
 is joined to its site, and kills are ledgered by the evidence they are
 (annotation sites counted, #30)

The defect, verbatim (Wesker 2fbd029): the census is 11 category rows of counts, with no stable
candidate-site ids (source location + AST role + source digest) and no total disposition per site and
operator; killed records carry `mutant_id`, `dimension`, `mutated_line` and `killed_by` but no site id and
no join to reach / install / entry / detection evidence; detection kills are not separated from
declared-contract kills in the ledger (the split exists only as the `killed_by` code); and annotation
sites are not classified: ARITHMETIC reads `generated: 2, withheld: 0` on a function with three
annotation BinOps (#30's one remaining item).

Why the obvious fix is wrong: a second walk that decides "generated" per site would be the second predicate
this repo treats as a defect class (#9). The site census runs the category's OWN recorders under a
ContextVar sink (`_SITE_SINK`), so each `_note` also reports the site it was noted at: the per-site
`generated` counts are the same notes the target count is made of, and the census checks that
`site_targets + function_level == category_targets` for every category on the whole fingerprint corpus.
The one class-level table (`CANDIDATE_CLASSES`, which node classes an operator reads) is guarded: no
mutant is ever joined to a (site, operator) pair the census does not list.

What each state of the pure decisions means. `site_disposition(candidate, annotation, targets, hold,
absent_reason)`: `not_applicable:not_a_candidate_class` (the node is not this operator's to answer);
`withheld:annotation` (in the annotation subtree #30 rules out, whatever else is true); `withheld:<hold>`
(the operator produced mutants and a policy hold suppressed them: `purity_overlay`, `one_sign_policy`);
`generated:`; else the reason the site gave nothing (`unsupported:name_sub_not_enrolled`,
`not_applicable:docstring` / `bare_reraise` / `already_return_none` / `not_isinstance` / ...), default
`not_applicable:no_alternative_at_site`. SWAP also records `withheld.pair_budget` and
`not_applicable.identical_operands` (#53) per call, and an unobserved single-type handler records
`withheld.unobserved_handler` (#37). `kill_class(killed_by, dimension, reach_dimensions)`: `contract`
(assertion, declared exception), `detection` (crash), `reach` (a dimension in `REACH_CLASS_DIMENSIONS`,
decided first so a reach-class kill can never be counted as a contract the suite declared), `unscored`
(any other recorded reason), `none`. `REACH_CLASS_DIMENSIONS` holds `OUTPUT:raise_inject`, the place for
the other lane's raise-inject kills.

Carried: `Mutant.site` (resolved once per `generate_mutants` by `SiteIndex`; a Form B wrapper is
`function`), `site` and `kill_class` on every killed/survivor/unscored record, and on `ProfilingResult` /
`--json`: `site_census`, `kill_ledger` (every class present including at 0; `kills` reconciles with
`total_killed`), and `mutant_ledger` (one row per executed mutant: site, disposition, outcome,
`reach_tests`, kill class; `reach_tests` is None when no line was reported, never 0). The rollup carries
`kill_ledger` merged over functions and `unledgered_functions` (a result with no ledger is counted, not
read as zeros). `category_census` rows gain `withheld_by` (`annotation`, `purity_overlay`,
`one_sign_policy`, `pair_budget`), appended after `disposition` so the row's existing key order and
`_census_row`'s output are untouched: before, a function with `a: int | None`, `b: int | str = 1 + 1`, a
`-> int | str` and an annotated local read ARITHMETIC `withheld: 0`; now `generated: 3, withheld: 4,
withheld_by: {annotation: 4}`. The policy id moves with the observation text only (universe unchanged):
10.2598eed3d331 -> 10.9a2fc78d0699, two-sign 10+neg.34638cf3c016 -> 10+neg.e3c781bee30b.

What was NOT closed: the human page does not print the ledger or the census (they are in `--json`, the
rollup and the result dict); a CLI line is the integrator's call. The census's `generated` per site is
per node, not per operator index inside a node (a Compare with two operators is one site with two
targets). `reach_tests` is the baseline's executed-line reach; admissible-vs-observed reach for each
mutant is not split in the row. The census is computed per profile call, not cached. Detective consumes
`killed_by` and `value_survivor_records` unchanged; whether declared-exception kills count in
degree-of-freedom pinning is a Detective-side accounting that this ledger makes checkable but does not
decide. The reach class has no producer until the other lane marks its raise-inject kills.

Receipt: not pinned here (the integrator re-pins `site_disposition`, `kill_class` and `is_candidate_class`
after Wesker's Wave 4 lands).
Tests: tests/test_site_census_intent.py (91 cases) plus the policy, exception, swap, canonical-id,
census, annotation, filter, engine, decorated-target, fresh-arguments, the generated `_census_row`
golden and the guard files: 500 passed under 3.14.6 and under 3.12.13, PYTHONUNBUFFERED unset. With the
annotation count, the site join and the kill split disarmed, 24 of the 91 fail. ruff clean under pinned
0.16.7.
